+
+## Misbehaving bots
+
+The limits are constants in `campfire_db::models::throttle` (no settings): `MAX_MESSAGES` (10) in
+`MESSAGES_WINDOW` (10 s), `COOLDOWN` (30 s), `MAX_COOLDOWN_ATTEMPTS` (5), `MAX_FAILED_DELIVERIES`
+(10).
+
+- State lives in two more `schema::ADDITIONS` tables, so it survives restarts and follows the
+  app's `Clock` (tests travel in time): `bot_throttles` (`campfire_db::Throttle`: `bot_id` unique,
+  `cooldown_ends_at`, `cooldown_attempts`, `failed_deliveries`) and `bot_suspensions`
+  (`campfire_db::Suspension`: `bot_id` unique, `reason` = `flooding` | `failing_webhook`).
+- Flooding counts the bot's own messages (`creator_id`, `created_at` newer than now − 10 s; the
+  added `index_messages_on_creator_id_and_created_at` keeps that cheap), so API posts and webhook
+  answers count alike without a counter. `Bot::admit_message` runs *inside the write transaction
+  that creates the message* (`messages::create_message_admitted`), so concurrent posts can't all
+  slip under the limit; a refusal returns `Ok(Err(admission))`, so the throttle's own writes
+  (starting a cooldown, counting an attempt, suspending) commit while no message is created.
+- The post over the limit starts the cooldown (`cooldown_attempts = 0`) and gets `429` with
+  `Retry-After: 30`. Every post during the cooldown, API or webhook answer, is an attempt: `429`
+  with the seconds left (rounded up), and the fifth suspends the bot (that fifth still answers
+  `429`; the next gets `403`). A cooldown after the previous one ended counts afresh.
+- Webhook answers refused by the throttle are dropped (logged at info). Webhooks are still
+  delivered during a cooldown; only suspension stops them.
+- `Answers::deliver` records every delivery (`Bot::record_delivery`): `WebhookError::is_failed_delivery`
+  is any error except `ReplyTooLarge` (that was a `2xx`). Success resets `failed_deliveries`; the
+  tenth failure in a row suspends.
+- Suspended: `messages::by_bots::ensure_not_suspended` answers `403` right after authentication
+  (before `set_room`); `Webhook::of_active_bots` leaves suspended bots out, so neither `mention`
+  nor `joined` reaches them. The user stays active, so rooms, messages, `Bot::count_created_by` and
+  the bots list are unchanged.
+- The bots list shows "Suspended" (a `<strong>`) and the reason
+  (`SuspensionReason::description`). Administrators get a "Reactivate" button (`button_to`
+  `DELETE /bots/:bot_id/suspension`, `bots/suspensions#destroy`, with `data-turbo-confirm`, which
+  Turbo shows with the native `confirm()`). Anyone else gets `403` there
+  (`ensure_can_administer`). `Bot::reactivate` deletes the suspension and the throttle row, so the
+  bot starts afresh; `Bot::destroy` does the same.
